  "body_html": "<h1>Trivial Representation as a Comodule</h1>\n<p>Let \\(R\\) be a commutative semiring, let \\(A\\) be a bialgebra over \\(R\\),\nand let \\(V\\) be an \\(R\\)-module. The <strong>trivial \\(A\\)-comodule</strong> on \\(V\\)\nhas coaction</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\rho(v) = v \\otimes 1.\n\\]</p>\n<p>This satisfies the axioms of\n<a class=\"node-ref\" data-node-id=\"linear_algebraic_groups.comodule_definition\" href=\"linear_algebraic_groups_comodule_definition.html\">an \\(A\\)-comodule</a>:\ncoassociativity follows from\n\\[\n\\Delta(1)=1\\otimes 1,\n\\]\nand the counit axiom follows from \\(\\varepsilon(1)=1\\).</p>\n<p>When \\(A = \\mathcal{O}(G)\\) is the coordinate Hopf algebra of an affine\ngroup scheme \\(G\\), this comodule corresponds to the representation on\nwhich every \\(R\\)-point of \\(G\\) acts by the identity on \\(V\\).</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
